  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote the garden app in `src/main.ts`. It passes `typecheck`, but I couldn't run `vite build` or open it in a browser, so the rendering and click mapping are untested.\n\n- **Scene:** a 24×24 soil ground with a wooden border sits under a gradient sky. A perspective camera at [0,18,21] looks at the plot. Lighting is a hemisphere light plus a shadow-casting sun with PCF soft shadows.\n- **Planting:** a `click` on the canvas is turned into a ray from the same camera constants and intersected with the plane y=0. Clicks that hit the sky or fall outside the ground are ignored. `window.__plantAt(x, z)` runs the same planting code, and returns false for non-finite or out-of-bounds coordinates.\n- **Growth:** each plant has its own start time and reaches full size over 8 s, so later plants are smaller. A sprout is a short light-green stem with two small leaves. It becomes a tall dark-green stem with four leaves and a green bud. The bud then opens into six petals around a gold centre. Petal colour, height and flower size vary per plant. A dark soil mound marks the spot from the first frame.\n- **Rendering cost:** all plants are drawn as five instanced nodes, so cost doesn't depend on plant count. The pool holds up to 300 plants, and clicks beyond that are ignored.\n- **Overlay and state:** a fixed top-left box shows `Plants: N` and a Clear button that removes all plants. `window.__TASK_STATE__` is a read-only object with `plantCount`, `plants` (`{x, z, growth}` computed live from the clock) and `ready`. `window.__EVAL_READY__` and `ready` are set after `app.ready()` and two animation frames.\n\nTwo assumptions could affect how it looks or behaves:\n- **Colour space:** I assumed per-instance RGBA colours are linear and converted from sRGB. If they are actually sRGB, colours will look slightly off.\n- **Picking math:** I assumed `fov` is the vertical field of view in degrees. I took that from the engine source. If it's wrong, planted spots would drift from the click position.",
